---
// Lesson 10.1e — 3-Button Jam: Revisions & Polish
// Execute P0/P1 revisions from friend playtests, verify each fix with a real follow-up
// test (catching regressions before adding polish), then add feedback juice and freeze.
import Lesson from '../../layouts/LessonLayout.astro';

const body = `<h1>10.1e — 3-Button Jam: Revisions &amp; Polish</h1>

<p class="lesson-lead">
    Playtesting without <strong>revising</strong> is just collecting bad news. Today you work
    straight down your <a href="10.1d.html">10.1d</a> triage list — fixing bugs and clarity
    issues first, confirming with a friend that your revision actually solved the confusion, and
    only <em>then</em> adding polish and freezing the build for Semester 1 Showcase.
</p>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="activity rpg">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">Step 1 — Execute P0 &amp; P1 Revisions (~30 min)</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~30 min</span>
    </div>

    <ol>
        <li><strong>Fix P0 blockers cleanly:</strong> resolve any soft-lock, off-screen trap, or retry-state leak where scores/timers fail to reset on <code>SceneManager.LoadScene()</code>.</li>
        <li><strong>Revise for first-10-second clarity (P1):</strong> if two testers missed Button 3 or misread hazards, fix the root cause in-game (bigger key prompt on HUD, higher color contrast between walkable vs lethal objects, slightly forgiving starting speed or wider safe zone on wave 1).</li>
        <li><strong>Verify with a Follow-Up Friend Check (mandatory):</strong> ask one of yesterday's testers to play <em>strictly after</em> your revision lands. Never assume your fix worked — watch them hit that exact moment again cleanly.</li>
    </ol>
</div>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="activity rpg">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">Step 2 — High-Leverage Feedback Polish &amp; Freeze (~25 min)</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~25 min</span>
    </div>

    <p>
        Once your P0/P1 verification test passes, pick <strong>two or three crisp feedback upgrades</strong>
        (not five new features!) that make your three buttons feel great:
    </p>

    <ul>
        <li><strong>Input response:</strong> tiny scale pop, color flash, or animation frame on the exact frame a button fires.</li>
        <li><strong>Readable threat &amp; score pops:</strong> distinct color change on hit, clear 0.3s warning flash before hazards fire, and unmistakable score increment.</li>
        <li><strong>Zero-friction loop:</strong> brief victory/loss state → instant single-button retry tested three times back-to-back.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="callout trap">
        <strong>Feature freeze rule:</strong> do not invent a brand-new mechanic on revision/polish day
        or refactor working systems right before Showcase. Every post-revision tweak MUST be
        re-played from Launch to Retry before you commit.
    </div>

    <div class="socratic">
        <h3>Socratic: Proving That a Revision Worked</h3>
        <ol>
            <li>Describe one P0 or P1 problem from your friend playtest, the exact code or scene change you made to revise it, and what happened differently when a tester re-played it.</li>
            <li>Did any revision accidentally introduce a side effect or new regression when you re-tested? How did re-playing catch it?</li>
            <li>Which single polish change (flash, scale feedback, sound cue, clearer HUD label) made the biggest jump in how your 3-button controls <em>feel</em>?</li>
        </ol>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="checklist">
    <h3>Checkpoint — before Showcase:</h3>
    <ul>
        <li>Ship every P0 and P1 revision from your friend playtest contract</li>
        <li>Verify your top revision in a follow-up test run with a classmate</li>
        <li>Add readability/feel polish without breaking the 3-button rule</li>
        <li>Run a clean full-loop smoke check (Start → Play → Win/Lose → Retry) and commit + push</li>
    </ul>
</div>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="resources">
    <h3>Reference Docs</h3>
    <p>Need a deeper explanation? These pages cover the same concepts:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-10/index.html">Unit 10: Jam Season</a> — revision &amp; polish checklist</li>
        <li><a href="10.1d.html">10.1d — Friend Playtest &amp; Triage</a> — the playtest evidence behind today's fixes</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Next: <a href="10.1f.html">10.1f — 3-Button Jam: Showcase &amp; Semester 1 Retro</a> — Finals-day Arcade Row showcase and Semester 1 retrospective.</p>
</div>`;
---
<Lesson id="10.1e" title="10.1e 3-Button Jam: Revisions &amp; Polish — AP CS Principles" root=".." css="../style.css">
  <Fragment set:html={body} />
</Lesson>
